### Phasor Noise `cop/phasornoise` (11 October 2026)

- Summary: Generates phasor noise, which resembles a wave pattern. (11 October 2026)
- Overview: This node generates various noises defined by phasor kernels. A phasor kernel is a local filter that defines sine and cosine waves in a small neighborhood around a center point. By default, the noise resembles a wave pattern. When the Signature is any channel except Mono, the node generates additional phasor noises for each component of the set channel and (11 October 2026)
- Inputs: pos (An optional UV layer with a value that's used instead of the pixel's image ...); time (An optional layer with a value that each pixel uses for the time.); bias (An optional layer with a value that's used for the peak position of each ...); scale (An optional layer with a value that's multiplied by the Element Size.); direction (An optional UV layer to set the initial angle of phasor kernels.) (11 October 2026)
- Outputs: noise (The computed noise.) (11 October 2026)
- Parm Signature (signature; String; default default): The layer type that the source outputs. (11 October 2026)
