### Pixelate `cop/pixelate` (11 October 2026)

- Summary: Increases the size of pixels to pixelate an input layer. (11 October 2026)
- Overview: This node pixelates an input layer by sampling the layer at a quantized position. The node enhances the size of individual pixels so you can see how many pixel blocks make up the image. The parameters on this node control the amount and size of the pixel blocks. Larger pixel blocks result in blurrier images. NOTE: The Blur COP in (11 October 2026)
- Inputs: source (The layer to pixelate.); effect (An optional per-pixel scaling amount of the Block Size parameter.); offset (An optional per-pixel addition to the Offset parameter.) (11 October 2026)
- Outputs: pixelate (The pixelated source layer.); blockid (An ID layer that contains a unique ID for each pixel block.) (11 October 2026)
- Parm Signature (signature; String; default auto): The layer type that the source accepts. (11 October 2026)
- Parm Mask (mask; Float; default 1): The amount of the new value to mix in with the original value. (11 October 2026)
- Parm Mode (mode; Menu; default 0) [Block Size | Number of Blocks]: The method used to determine the amount of pixel blocks. (11 October 2026)
- Parm Units (units; Menu; default 0) [Image | Pixels]: When Mode is Block Size, this is the unit of measurement used to determine the Block Size. (11 October 2026)
- Parm Block Size (blocksize, blocksize_pixel; Float; default 0.03): The size in image coordinates or pixels of the resulting pixel block, which determines how many blocks appear along the X and Y-axes. (11 October 2026)
- Parm Element Scale (elementscalex, elementscaley, elementscale_pixelx ...): When the Smallicon:BUTTONS/decompose_transforms Per-Component Controls button is on, this is the per-axis scaling of the element size for the pixel block. (11 October 2026)
