### Time Loop `cop/timeloop` (11 October 2026)

- Summary: Repeats input frame range to form a looping animation. (11 October 2026)
- Overview: This node will repeat the time evaluated on the input to create a looping output sequence. It can also blend the input over time to avoid a harsh seam. In blend mode, the input sequence is offset by half the interval and the original and offset are blended together to hide the point where the sequence wraps. (11 October 2026)
- Inputs: source (The VDB, Layer, or Attribute to loop.) (11 October 2026)
- Outputs: loop (The input re-timed into a looping sequence.) (11 October 2026)
- Parm Signature (signature; String; default auto): The layer type that the source accepts. (11 October 2026)
- Parm Frame Start (fstart; Int; default 1): The frame to start the looping sequence at. (11 October 2026)
- Parm Frame Length (flen; Int; default 24): The length of the sequence to loop, in frames. (11 October 2026)
- Parm Loop Type (type; Menu; default 0) [Cycle | Zig-Zag | Blend]: How to loop the sequence. (11 October 2026)
- Parm Blend Shape (blendshape; Menu; default 0) [Linear | Cosine]: How to blend in the offset sequence. (11 October 2026)
