##### Tile Generator (11 October 2026)
- Category: Texture generators > Patterns (11 October 2026)
- Height relevance: high (11 October 2026)
- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/substance-graphs/nodes-reference-for-substance-graphs/node-library/texture-generators/patterns/tile-generator (11 October 2026)
- Purpose: The workhorse pattern node: repeats a chosen shape or up to six custom input patterns on an X by Y grid, with per-tile control of size, offset, rotation, value and masking. It is described as one of the most advanced nodes of the library. (11 October 2026)
- Inputs: Pattern Input 1-6 (Grayscale Input); Background (Grayscale Input) (11 October 2026)
- Key parameters: (11 October 2026)
  - `X Amount` (1 to 64): Number of tile repetitions along X. (11 October 2026)
  - `Y Amount` (1 to 64): Number of tile repetitions along Y. (11 October 2026)
  - `Pattern` (Image Input, Square, Disc, Paraboloid, Bell, Gaussian, Thorn, Pyramid, Brick, Gradation, Waves, Half Bell, Ridged Bell, Crescent, Capsule, Cone): The tile shape, one of the built-in height profiles or Image Input for custom patterns. (11 October 2026)
  - `Pattern Specific` (0.0 to 1.0): Morphs the selected built-in shape (the effect depends on which pattern is chosen). (11 October 2026)
  - `Size Mode` (Normal / Interstice, Normal / Size, Keep Ratio, Absolute, Pixel): How tile size is defined (the Normal modes by interstice or by size, Keep Ratio, Absolute, Pixel). (11 October 2026)
  - `Interstice X/Y` (0.0 to 1.0): Gap between tiles, only in the interstice size mode. (11 October 2026)
  - `Scale` (0.0 to 2.0): Global scale of every tile. (11 October 2026)
  - `Scale Random` (0.0 to 1.0): Random scale variation per tile. (11 October 2026)
  - `Offset` (0.0 to 1.0): Incremental shift applied row after row (or column after column), which gives running-bond brick layouts. (11 October 2026)
  - `Position Random` (0.0 to 1.0): Random per-tile displacement, with separate X and Y control. (11 October 2026)
  - `Rotation [Rotation]` (0.0 to 1.0): Free rotation applied to all tiles. (11 October 2026)
  - `Rotation Random [Rotation]` (0.0 to 1.0): Random free rotation per tile. (11 October 2026)
  - `Luminance/Color Random` (0.0 to 1.0): Per-tile luminance variation, i.e. random tile heights in a height graph. (11 October 2026)
  - `Checker Mask` (False/True): Hides every other tile in a checkerboard fashion. (11 October 2026)
  - `Random Mask` (0.0 to 1.0): Randomly hides a proportion of tiles. (11 October 2026)
  - `Blending Mode` (Add, Max, Add Sub): How overlapping tiles combine (Add, Max, Add Sub). (11 October 2026)
- Other parameters (names only): `Non Square Expansion`, `Pattern Input Number`, `Pattern Input Distribution`, `Image Input Filtering (Engine >v4 only)`, `Rotation [Pattern]`, `Rotation Random [Pattern]`, `Quincunx Flip`, `Symmetry Random`, `Symmetry Random Mode`, `Middle Size`, `Size (Absolute/Pixel)`, `Scale Random Seed`, `Offset Random`, `Offset Random Seed`, `Vertical Offset`, `Global Offset`, `Color`, `Luminance By Number`, `Luminance By Scale`, `Horizontal Mask`, `Vertical Mask`, `Invert Mask`, `Background Color`, `Global Opacity`, `Reverse Rendering Order` (11 October 2026)
- Typical use in a height graph: Bricks, tiles, cobblestones, shingles, planks and any repeated module in a height graph; run its output into Flood Fill or Edge Detect to drive per-tile randomisation, bevels and wear. (11 October 2026)
- Copernicus 22 equivalent: `tilepattern`. Set **Mode** to Tile Count and fill **Rows**/**Columns** (X Amount, Y Amount), or Seamless with **Divisions** for guaranteed tiling; **Pattern Type**=Stack Bond gives a square grid, Stretcher Bond gives the brick offset (also **Row Slide Offset** with a **Variation**); **Inset** is the interstice; **Draw As** chooses Filled, Distance (bevel-like falloff with **Fade Distance**), Gradient (with **Gradient Ramp** and **Rotate**) or Outline; **Tile Value** with **Variation** is the per-tile luminance; **Uniform Scale** plus **Variation** randomise size; **Rotate Tile** plus **Rotate Variation** randomise rotation; **Uniform Jitter** randomises position; masks are **Every Nth Tile**, **Checkerboard** and the **Threshold** prune group. Custom patterns go into the `stamp0` input; outputs are `tiles` output, `id` output (per-tile ID for random values) and `uv` output (per-tile UV). (11 October 2026)
- Equivalence status: SideFX-confirmed at node level (the SideFX Copernicus for Substance 3D Designer users page lists this correspondence), parameter setup read from the local Houdini 22.0.368 node help (11 October 2026)

