  - `Offset` (0.0 to 1.0): Translation, snapped so pixels are not interpolated. (11 October 2026)
  - `Rotation` (0.0 to 1.0): Rotation of the input. (11 October 2026)
  - `Tile Safe Rotation` (False/True): Snaps the rotation to safe values that do not blur pixels. (11 October 2026)
  - `Symmetry` (none, X, Y, X+Y): Optional mirroring (none, X, Y, X+Y). (11 October 2026)
  - `Mipmap Mode` (Automatic, Manual): Automatic or manual mipmapping. (11 October 2026)
  - `Mipmap Level` (0 to 10): Manual mipmap level (0 to 10). (11 October 2026)
- Other parameters (names only): `Background Color` (11 October 2026)
- Typical use in a height graph: Varying the scale or offset of a tiling noise or height while staying seamless; the standard way to reuse one noise in several scales. (11 October 2026)
- Copernicus 22 equivalent: `xform2d` with **Border**=Wrap (tiling), **Uniform Scale** equal to 1 over Tile, **Translate** for Offset, **Rotate** (multiples of 90 degrees are lossless), and **Filter** set to a point or nearest option to avoid interpolation blur. Mipmap control has no direct switch. Exact snapping behaviour UNVERIFIED. (11 October 2026)
