##### Quadrant (FX-Map node) (11 October 2026)
- Category: Function graph nodes (11 October 2026)
- Height relevance: high (11 October 2026)
- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-designer/using/substance-function-graphs/fx-maps/the-quadrant-node (11 October 2026)
- Purpose: The most powerful FX-Map node: it subdivides the FX-Map image into four parts for the next node of the chain, is the only node that increases the depth (octave) of the underlying quad-tree, and draws an optional pattern at its position. (11 October 2026)
- Note: Parameters documented by Adobe: Branch Offset, Pattern (input image or built-in shapes such as Square, Disc, Bell, Gaussian, Thorn, Pyramid, Brick, Waves, Capsule), Pattern Offset, Pattern Size, Pattern Rotation, Pattern Variation, Blending Mode, Random Seed and Inherit Random; most can be driven by a dynamic function graph. A Quadrant node can only render a grayscale input into a grayscale FX-Map and a colour input into a colour FX-Map. (11 October 2026)
- Key parameters: (11 October 2026)
  - `Branch Offset` (transform): Shifts the node image and every image rendered below it in the same branch. (11 October 2026)
  - `Pattern` (input image or built-in shape): Image drawn by this node (none by default). (11 October 2026)
  - `Pattern Size` (Float2): Size of the drawn pattern. (11 October 2026)
  - `Pattern Rotation` (Float): Rotation of the drawn pattern. (11 October 2026)
  - `Blending Mode` (choice): Blending of this image into the FX-Map image. (11 October 2026)
  - `Random Seed` (Integer): Seed of the random sequence. (11 October 2026)
  - `Inherit Random` (Boolean): Takes the seed from the previous node. (11 October 2026)
- Typical use in a height graph: Recursive placement of patterns (multi-scale rock or crack layouts, subdivided tilings, random scatter at several octaves). (11 October 2026)
- Copernicus 22 equivalent: No single node. A quad-tree subdivision can be generated as points in SOPs (or with `pointgenerate`) and stamped with `stamppoint` or `shapescatter` (**Blend Method**=Maximum), with per-level scale and rotation set by `configurestamps`; the recursion logic itself is VEX or Python. UNVERIFIED chain. (11 October 2026)
