##### A3 Generators (11 October 2026)

- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/generators/generator (11 October 2026)
- SOURCE: a generator is a substance that builds a mask or texture from the mesh topology using baked utility maps such as Position, Curvature and World Space Normal; most outputs are black and white, so generators mostly drive masks, and they are added by right-clicking a mask or a layer, choosing Add generator, then picking the generator with the Generator button in the Properties panel (11 October 2026)
- Reading rule for this section: a Painter generator needs a mesh; for a flat tiling height texture the same masks are derived from the height itself, with `curvature`, `heighttoambientocclusion`, `heighttonormal`, `ramp` and noise nodes (the skeleton is given in A3.10) (11 October 2026)

###### A3.1 Dirt (11 October 2026)
- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/generators/dirt (11 October 2026)
- Purpose: builds a black-and-white buildup of dirt and grunge in crevices, along edges and on flat areas from curvature and ambient occlusion, optionally refined by micro height and micro normal inputs (11 October 2026)
- Baked maps needed: Position, Curvature, Ambient Occlusion, World Space Normal; optional inputs Custom Grunge, Micro Normal, Micro Height (each a texture or an anchor point) (11 October 2026)
- Key parameters: Seed, Invert, Dirt Level, Dirt Contrast, Use Triplanar, Triplanar Blending Contrast, Grunge Amount, Grunge Scale, Use Custom Grunge, Edges Masking (how strongly edges mask out dirt, from the curvature map); Micro Details: Micro Height, Micro Normal, Curvature Type (Standard is sharp and can miss broad detail, Sobel is slightly blurrier, Smooth blurs at several levels and can lose detail), Curvature Intensity, Height Details Intensity, AO Radius, AO Depth (11 October 2026)
- Height role (UNVERIFIED reading): the mask says where deposit height is added (dust, mud) or where pits are cut; the Micro Height input injects fine bump detail into the mask itself (11 October 2026)
- COP chain, UNVERIFIED: `curvature` (Output Type Concavity) -> `blend` Multiply with an inverted `heighttoambientocclusion` -> `blend` Add or Maximum with grunge from `fractalnoise` or `grunge_layerednoise` (Grunge Amount = the Mask parameter, Grunge Scale = Element Size) -> `remap` Operation Threshold (Dirt Level = Threshold, Dirt Contrast = inverse of Width) -> optional `blur`; to deposit height, `blend` Add of mask times a depth constant (11 October 2026)

###### A3.2 Metal Edge Wear (11 October 2026)
- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/generators/metal-edge-wear (11 October 2026)
- Purpose: simulates damage and scratches on the parts of a mesh most likely to be knocked, as a black-and-white mask (11 October 2026)
- Baked maps needed: Position, Curvature (defines the edges), Ambient Occlusion, World Space Normal; optional Custom Grunge, Micro Normal, Micro Height (11 October 2026)
- Key parameters: Seed, Invert, Wear Level, Wear Contrast, Use Triplanar, Triplanar Blending Contrast, Grunge Amount, Grunge Scale, Use Custom Grunge, Edges Smoothness, Ambient Occlusion Masking (occluded areas get no wear), Curvature Weight (very low values keep only grunge); Micro Details identical to Dirt (11 October 2026)
- Height role (UNVERIFIED reading): wear mask times a chip depth is the standard way to carve edge chips into a height; the same mask drives roughness and metal elsewhere (11 October 2026)
- COP chain, UNVERIFIED: `curvature` (Output Type Convexity) -> `remap` Threshold (Wear Level and Wear Contrast) -> `blend` Multiply by (1 minus occlusion) for AO masking -> breakup with `fractalnoise` or `grunge_galvanizedsteel` -> `blur` for Edges Smoothness -> `blend` Subtract from the height; scratches with `streakblur` on a `randommono` set to Random per Pixel; chips with `shapescatter` whose `density` input is the wear mask (11 October 2026)

###### A3.3 Fiber Glass Edge Wear (11 October 2026)
- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/generators/fiber-glass-edge-wear (11 October 2026)
- Purpose: black-and-white mask for worn and frayed edges on fiberglass; the Designer counterpart note says it could suit cloth (11 October 2026)
- Baked maps needed: Curvature, Ambient Occlusion, World Space Normal, Position; optional Micro Height, Micro Normal, Custom Grunge (11 October 2026)
- Key parameters: Seed, Invert (flips internal maps such as curvature or AO before they combine), Wear Level, Wear Contrast, Use Triplanar, Triplanar Blending Contrast, Grunge Amount, Use Custom Grunge, Edges Smoothness, Ambient Occlusion Masking, Curvature Weight; Micro Details as in Dirt (11 October 2026)
- Height role (UNVERIFIED reading): frayed rims, fibers that stand proud or are cut at an edge (11 October 2026)
- COP chain, UNVERIFIED: same chain as Metal Edge Wear plus a short `streakblur` (Mode Max or Blur, small Length) along the edge direction to give a frayed look (11 October 2026)

###### A3.4 Mask Editor (11 October 2026)
- Source: https://experienceleague.adobe.com/en/docs/substance-3d-painter/using/effects/generators/mask-editor (11 October 2026)
