#### Group F: Binders, coatings and pavement (11 October 2026)

Mineral pastes applied or cast, and the road surfaces made from aggregate and binder; their relief is low and comes from the tool (trowel, form, dash) or from what the paste holds (pores, aggregate, cracks), so stampers and thresholded noises dominate the recipes (11 October 2026)

##### F1 Plaster (11 October 2026)

- **Macro**: a wall plane with slight hand-applied waviness; lime plaster is calcium hydroxide with sand that sets by carbonation, gypsum plaster expands slightly as it sets, clay plaster with fibres was applied in thick base coats and shrinks, cracks and distorts on drying when too plastic, and cement plaster is used on masonry for a smooth surface [S1] (11 October 2026)
- **Meso**: trowel marks as overlapping flat fan-shaped strokes with small ridges at their edges, map cracking on old lime work (UNVERIFIED, the source does not cover trowel finishes or crack patterns) (11 October 2026)
- **Micro**: fine sand of the finish coat; historic lime top coats were thin veneers, often 1/8 in or less [S1] (11 October 2026)
- **Period**: none (11 October 2026)
- **Joints**: none (11 October 2026)
- **Profile**: plateaus from trowel strokes with small lips at the stroke edges, otherwise smooth (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Histogram**: narrow, with a slight positive skew from the lips (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Spectrum**: low energy, a steep slope from the smoothness plus a small high-frequency sand band (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Anisotropy**: stroke directions vary, weak global anisotropy (11 October 2026)
- **Components**: stroke regions bounded by lips; cracks as a sparse connected network (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Recipe**, start values UNVERIFIED: (11 October 2026)
- L1 Macro, wall waviness: `fractalnoise` [Perlin, Element Size half the canvas, Amplitude 0.05]; SD: clouds_2 (11 October 2026)
- L2 Meso, trowel strokes: stamps made from `sdfshape` [Rectangle, Round Corners 0.4] > `wrangle` flat plateau with a lip on the trailing edge, scattered by `shapescatter` [Scale Variance 0.4, Angle Variance 180, Blend Method Depth-Sorted Over so that later strokes cover earlier ones, Do Tiled on]; how Depth-Sorted Over composites Mono heights is UNVERIFIED, fall back to Maximum; SD: Tile Sampler with a stroke shape and random rotation (11 October 2026)
- L3 Meso, map cracks: two `worleynoise` borders at two sizes, sparse and thin, subtracted at 0.01; SD: cells_1 with histogram_scan (11 October 2026)
- L4 Micro, sand: `randommono` [Random per Pixel] > `blur` [Units Pixels, Size 0.5] at 0.003; SD: White Noise (11 October 2026)
- **Tileable**: Do Tiled on `shapescatter`, Tile Size on the noises (11 October 2026)
- **Pitfalls**: plaster read through a single noise looks like stucco or concrete; the strokes and their lips are the cue (11 October 2026)
- **Sources**: [S1] https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plaster ; [S2] https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/worleynoise.html (11 October 2026)

