##### F3 Concrete (smooth, cast with formwork, broken) (11 October 2026)

- **Macro, formed**: plywood forms are most commonly 3/4 in or 18 mm thick, modular slab systems use modules no larger than 1 to 2 m, column forms use 20 mm through bolts, wall forms are held by twin steel walers and tie bolts, and board-formed concrete such as the Royal National Theatre carries the impression of the timber shuttering [S1]; panel seams, tie hole grids and board steps make the large-scale pattern (spacings UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Meso, formed**: bugholes are small regular or irregular cavities usually under 15 mm in diameter, from air bubbles trapped at the surface during placement and consolidation, common on vertical walls, columns and beams, their number and size depending on the form, the release agent, the mix and the consolidation [S2]; form oil reduces adhesion between the form and the concrete [S1] (11 October 2026)
- **Macro and meso, broken**: fracture faces with exposed aggregate, cracks, spalls and rebar (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Micro**: cement paste with fine sand; plywood or board grain imprinted in reverse (11 October 2026)
- **Period**: tie holes and panel seams form a large lattice; board-formed concrete has a 1D period across the boards (11 October 2026)
- **Joints**: thin fins or steps at panel and board seams (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Profile**: flat with hemispherical bugholes, cylindrical tie recesses, small fins; board steps of a few mm; broken concrete is faceted (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Histogram**: a narrow peak with a negative tail from bugholes for formed concrete, broad for broken concrete (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Spectrum**: a nearly flat high-frequency band from pores on formed faces; a fracture slope near minus 3.6 for broken faces is UNVERIFIED (11 October 2026)
- **Anisotropy**: strong across the boards for board-formed concrete, weak otherwise (11 October 2026)
- **Components**: bugholes as many small black components, denser near the top of each pour and on sloped forms (density zones UNVERIFIED); tie holes as a regular lattice of equal components (11 October 2026)
- **Recipe**, start values UNVERIFIED unless quoted from the local concrete module: (11 October 2026)
