##### F4 Asphalt (11 October 2026)

- **Macro**: a road plane with ruts, rectangular patches and crack networks; fatigue (crocodile) cracking starts as thin sparse longitudinal cracks along the traffic, then transverse cracks connect them into sharp-sided prism-shaped pieces, and the severe stage pumps out fines, spalls the edges, and leads to potholes and cracks of 3/8 in or wider; crescent-shaped edge cracks appear near weak shoulders [S1] (11 October 2026)
- **Meso**: crocodile cells can reach 300 mm across and are typically under 150 mm [S1]; aggregate stones protruding from the bitumen matrix; stripping or raveling, the loss of adhesion between asphalt and aggregate, thins the pavement [S1] (aggregate sizes UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Micro**: fine aggregate and sand, polished stone tops on worn lanes (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Period**: none (11 October 2026)
- **Joints**: cracks act as joints, V shaped with spalled edges (11 October 2026)
- **Profile**: domed or angular stone tops proud of a low matrix; cracks as V notches (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Histogram**: negative skew from the voids for open-graded mixes, near Gaussian for dense mixes (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Spectrum**: a bump at the aggregate size over a slope near minus 3 (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Anisotropy**: isotropic, except ruts and longitudinal cracks along the traffic (11 October 2026)
- **Components**: white stones as many lognormal components, black connected matrix; crack cells under 150 mm (11 October 2026)
- **Recipe**, start values UNVERIFIED: (11 October 2026)
- L1 Meso, aggregate: two `shapescatter` passes [dense, Scale Variance 0.6, Angle Variance 180, Blend Method Maximum, Do Tiled on] of angular stamps from `sdfshape` [Polygon, 5 to 7 sides] > `planarinflate` at a low Height Scale, the second pass at half the size; SD: Tile Sampler or Splatter (11 October 2026)
- L2 Meso, binder: a `blur` of the aggregate layer, scaled and lowered, merged with Maximum so stones look embedded rather than stacked; SD: blur_hq_grayscale and Blend Max (11 October 2026)
- L3 Meso, wear: a soft top clamp in a `wrangle` polishes stone tops; raveled holes from `randommono` on the stamp id > `remap` [Operation Threshold, Threshold 0.95] removing whole stones; SD: levels, Flood Fill to Random Grayscale (11 October 2026)
