- **Sources**: [S1] https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crocodile_cracking ; [S2] https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/worleynoise.html (11 October 2026)

#### Group G: Metal and hard surface (11 October 2026)

Rolled, brushed, hammered and pressed metal and the panel language of hard-surface design; many of these are strictly periodic (corrugation, tread plate, mail) and are best identified by M1 and M4, while brushed and rusted metal are identified by M6 and M7 (11 October 2026)

##### G1 Rusted metal (11 October 2026)

- **Macro**: sheet or plate with dents, raised rust blisters under paint, delaminating rust scale and holes (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Meso**: pitting attacks an otherwise passive surface at sizes from microns to millimetres, in random small holes whose density grows along a sigmoid through induction, propagation and saturation; pits start at scratches, local alloy changes, sulfide inclusions and damaged coatings, polished surfaces resist pitting better, and corrosion products often hide the pits [S1] (11 October 2026)
- **Micro**: granular rust crust, stepped flakes of scale (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Period**: none (11 October 2026)
- **Joints**: none; seams and rivets belong to G4 and G7 (11 October 2026)
- **Profile**: blisters as domes, pits deep and narrow, scale as stacked thin plates with steps (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Histogram**: positive skew from crust and blisters with a negative tail from pits; multimodal where scale layers stack (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Spectrum**: broadband near minus 3 (UNVERIFIED) (11 October 2026)
- **Anisotropy**: isotropic; vertical streaks on weathered walls (11 October 2026)
- **Components**: rust patches clustered at high thresholds, pits as many small black components (11 October 2026)
- **Recipe**, start values UNVERIFIED unless quoted from the local painted metal recipe: (11 October 2026)
- L1 Macro, plate and dents: `constant` plus a sparse `shapescatter` of shallow inverted domes; SD: Uniform Color plus Shape Splatter (11 October 2026)
- L2 Meso, rust coverage: `grunge_rustysurface` [Primary Roughness, Secondary Roughness, Cracks Mask, Cracks Size, Seed] or `grunge_rust`, remapped into a coverage mask; SD: rust grunge maps (11 October 2026)
- L3 Meso, crust relief: `fractalnoise` [Fractal Type Hybrid Terrain or Sharp, granular Element Size] times the mask, blisters from a `worleynoise` dist1 inverted into domes inside the mask, scale steps from `quantize` [Segments 3 to 4] of the crust then `blur` [Size 1 pixel]; SD: clouds_3, cells_1, Quantize Grayscale (11 October 2026)
- L4 Micro, pits: `shapescatter` of tiny pits [Blend Method Minimum, Density layer mask the rust mask], or `randommono` [Random per Pixel] thresholded and dilated; SD: BnW Spots, Blend Min (11 October 2026)
- L5 Meso, paint remnants on painted metal: the local recipe uses a perlin_noise at scale 3 blurred by 10 and clipped between 0.4 and 0.6 for the domed enamel, cells_1 at scale 8 thresholded at 1 minus the chip density for flakes, a perlin_noise at scale 16 driving a warp for dents, and a perlin_noise at scale 48 added at 0.06 for scratches (Copernicus1.md lines 1315 to 1319); the paint edge gets the lip of E4 L5; SD: as quoted (11 October 2026)
- **Tileable**: Tile Size on the grunge nodes and noises, Do Tiled on `shapescatter` (11 October 2026)
